'''Summer Sweep Up - Batch II'''

'''Agility Changes:'''
<u>The Hallowed Sepulchre</u>

* Lowered the Floor 4 entry requirement to '''Level 77''', down from 82.
* Lowered the Floor 5 entry requirement to '''Level 87''', down from 92.
* You can now boost for Floor entry. For example, a player at 72 Agility can eat a bite of a Summer pie at the end of Floor 3 to gain entry to Floor 4.
* Floor 5's Grand Coffin now requires 84 Thieving ''or'' 92 Agility to open. Boosting can be used for both requirements.

<u>Colossal Wyrm Agility course</u>

* Increased the duration of the Colossal Wyrm Agility course:
** The basic course by ~25%.
** The advanced course by ~40%.
* Increased XP, Bone shards and Termites to match so that it's roughly the same XP/hr and termites/hr but fewer inputs/hr, meaning the course is lower intensity than before.

<u>New Agility Shortcuts</u>

* Level 49 - There is now a small gap in the west side of the Draynor Manor fence that you can pass through.
* Level 52 - Added stepping stones across the River Lum, just south of the Champion's Guild.
* Level 54 - You can now use the new shortcut on the south-west side of Giant's Plateau to climb up and down, providing easy access to and from the desert.
* Level 60 - Added a pipe at the southern edge of Edgeville Dungeon, cutting down on travel time if you've lost your Brass key.
* Level 52 & 62 - This new shortcut at the central area of the top and middle floors of the Arceuus Library allows you to jump down to the bottom floor.
* Level 79 - Located north of Sophanem, we've added stepping stones for those of you who need to cross the River Elid in a flash.
* Level 82 - Thanks to these new stepping stones at the small island north of Mos le'Harmless, your least favourite Treasure Trail step just got a whole lot better.
* Level 83 - Added a shortcut west of Pollnivneach, allowing quick access from Ali the Hag's hut to the nearby plateau.

Adjustments to several grapple/crossbow shortcuts so they no longer require any equipment to use: (As a result, their level requirements have been increased accordingly.) Keep in mind that any Achievement Diary tasks that involve a grapple shortcut will still require you to use the grapple to complete the task.

* Level 8 Grapple - The broken raft in River Lum can now be used barehanded at Level 48.
* Level 11 Grapple - The Falador rough wall can now be climbed barehanded at Level 52.
* Level 32 Grapple - The rock-climb between Catherby and Taverley can now be used barehanded at Level 68. We've also made this a two-way shortcut.
* Level 36 Grapple - You can now cross between the Water Obelisk island and Catherby barehanded at''' '''Level 72.
* Level 39 Grapple - The Yanille rough wall can now be climbed barehanded at Level 69.
* Level 53 Grapple - Strong trees just south of Karamja Volcano can now be used barehanded at Level 78.

<u>Additional Agility improvements:</u>

* Slightly opened up the fence around the Clock Tower, allowing you to pass through a new gap and walk around the building.
* Zaryte crossbow will now be recognised as suitable to use for Crossbow Agility shortcuts.

'''Miscellaneous Improvements:'''

* Knight Waves Training Ground no longer resets your progress if you leave the trial using the door.
* Reduced Chivalry's drain rate to match Deadeye and Mystic Vigour, draining 1 point per 3 seconds.
* Removed thrall immunity from Menaphite Akh in Beneath Cursed Sands.
* Removed the timeout/cooldown on making parties at the Theatre of Blood.
* Lowered the Light & Heavy Ranged Defence for Abyssal Guardians and Abyssal Walkers to '''0''', down from 70 and 75 respectively.
* Lowered the Crush Defence for Abyssal Guardians to '''0''', down from 70.
* You can now re-enter the Fight Caves immediately after leaving, with no cooldown.
* Increased the drop rate of the Rune Essence Pouch:
** From Abyssal Guardian: up to '''1 in 8''' from 1 in 42.
** From Abyssal Walker: up to '''1 in 5''' from 1 in 42.
* Bonfire changes:
** Added a "Tend to" option to add more logs to a bonfire.
** If you have one type of log in your inventory, the 'Make-X' interface will no longer appear when you use a log on an existing bonfire.
** If you have more than one type of logs in your inventory, the 'Make-X' interface will appear
** Instead, you can use the logs to start adding, and either click away or keep going until you run out of logs.
** Hand-warming animation will no longer persist once you run out of logs.

'''Chambers of Xeric Loot Changes:'''

* Adjusted the weighting of various unique rewards in both Normal and Challenge Mode Chambers of Xeric. Check the main body of the blog for a more detailed write-up and table.

'''Wyrmscraig Changes'''

* Upon defeating The Mad Angel during the Fallen From Grace quest, players will now be granted a killcount for the Mad Angel. Players who have already defeated the boss during the quest will receive the killcount retroactively upon logging in.
* The Mad Angel now drops Medium clues instead of Hard ones.
* The Mad Angel's clue drops now persist on the ground for the usual 3 hours.
* Gems dropped from Golem Crafting will now go straight into an open Gem Bag, if you have one. Otherwise they'll fall to the floor as before.
* Mr McGroot has been removed from the Skilling Pets section of the Collection Log, as he is only obtainable through Goat Hunting rather than the Hunting skill as a whole, which is inconsistent with other Skilling Pets.
* Using the Jeweller's Chisel on Sunlight Antelope antlers now works without issues.
* Ocean random events will no longer spawn in inaccessible areas of Wyrmscraig.
* The stile on Wyrmscraig no longer requires players to complete The Fremennik Trials to cross.
* We've shared the Wyrmscraig drop rates - find out more in its dedicated section.

Additional Sailing Changes:

* Super fishing potions can now be stored inside the Tackle box.
* Corrected the messaging displayed when using the "Teleport to boat" spell on boats without a Greater Teleport Focus.

'''Other Changes'''

* Maggot King's Speed Chaser Combat Achievement has been moved up to Grandmaster tier to better reflect the task's actual difficulty, as mentioned in <u>[https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/a=13/wyrmscraig--sailing-changes?oldschool=1#BMR last week's game update blog]</u>. You might need to speak to Ghommal/Laidee Gnonock again to reobtain your Grandmaster Helm..
* Sotfa Forest’s blood-hungry snail has now been enabled. It’s only accepting group bookings, and the guests are on the menu...
* The northernmost Red Salamander spot at Ourania Altar now allows you to complete the Hard Ardougne Achievement Diary task.
* The Chugging Barrel can now be used when you're near Eniola (the Ourania Altar banker), or the Wyrmscraig bank chest (provided you've built it) or the Lumbridge bank chest (on PvP worlds where it appears).
* The Portal Nexus will no longer teleport you to the wrong destination after changing your configured teleports.
* The Runecraft skill guide has been updated to remove an incorrect listing.
* Various items have had the capitalisation of their names corrected, starting with pets like Mr McGroot, along with some god-themed items. More will follow in subsequent updates.

'''PvP Rota'''

The PvP rota has moved to '''Period A''':

* 539 - (US) - PvP World
* 318 - (UK) - Bounty Hunter World
* 548 - (Germany) - High-Risk PvP World
* 577 - (US) - Free-to-Play PvP World
* 559 - (UK) - LMS Competitive

World 390 (AUS) for LMS Competitive has been '''<u>activated</u>''' with this rota.

World 569 (AUS) for Bounty Hunter has been '''<u>activated</u>''' with this rota.

The PvP Arena is using '<b>Zerker</b>' loadouts in Ranked Duels and Tournaments this week.

