===Chambers of Xeric Loot Changes===
Chambers of Xeric unique weightings have been a hot topic for almost as long as the raid has existed, and this Summer Sweep-Up we'd sought to make further changes to address one of the most frequent complaints regarding the volume of purple lights that become Prayer scrolls.

As we wrapped up our initial Sweep-Up blogs, we'd said that we'd like to take a conservative approach here and adjust incrementally over time. It would be an understatement to say that this wasn't a particularly popular stance to take, so a few weeks ago we proposed more radical for adjustments to the weightings of uniques in the Chambers of Xeric. These numbers make CoX a little more in-line with other raids when it comes to how many hours the content expects you to put in. They look like big shifts and in many cases they ''are ''big shifts but we believe they could make for a healthier raid long-term.

The most significant shift here is Ancestral pieces, which do fetch a hefty price currently, but also serve as a huge source of frustration since ticking off the full set takes considerably longer on average than a Twisted Bow.

Realistically these numbers are a big enough shift that it's impossible to predict exactly where things might shake out now that they're implemented, but we do expect that while individual item prices might shift, the GP/hr of the raid shouldn't drastically reduce. These changes aim to bring regular Chambers completions more in line with other raids while also improving the value proposition offered by Challenge Mode clears compared to regular raids.

